    "notes": "Root inspected source and six native views. Dozebear is a low broad drowsy quadruped with a heavy eyelid and mostly closed dream slit; Denumbra stands upright on massive hind paws with high stepped shoulder mantle and a vertical open chest den. Forearms, stance, body proportions and den development differ substantially. Rear views retain smooth low shoulders versus tall pointed mantle; both face upper right and omit chest-face duplication. Nine guarded middle-stage face pixels and thirteen final-stage face pixels preserve eyelid, pupils and separate embedded dream eyes. Area-vote chosen over noisy source-center. Densy recipe retained. Exact palettes and clear native borders.",
